WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.279
Marvel famously plays their cards close to
the vest when it comes to keeping story details

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.760
secret...both to avoid spoilers and to keep
fans guessing.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.080
But the studio has revealed some unexpected
characters set to appear in its next big film.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.600
Here's a look at some of the most surprising
characters confirmed for Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.960
And, obviously, some major potential spoilers
ahead.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.699
Portrayed by Tilda Swinton in 2016's Doctor
Strange, the Ancient One was Stephen Strange's

00:00:28.699 --> 00:00:33.740
mentor who taught the eventual Sorcerer Supreme
everything he knows about magic and the mystic

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:34.240
arts.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.980
In the film, it's revealed that she'd been
using dark magic to lengthen her life.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.680
"She draws power from the dark dimension to stay alive"

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.920
That's not true I've seen the rituals, worked them

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:48.420
out."

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.020
Soon after, in a savage battle with villain
Kaecilius, the Ancient One is mortally wounded

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:54.640
and dies.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.160
But not before a final heart-to-heart with
Strange via astral projection.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:04.220
While death isn't always the end of the road
in superhero movies, the images of the Ancient

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:08.939
One's vanishing astral projection seemed as
final an outcome as one can receive in the

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:09.440
MCU.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:15.400
That's exactly why many fans were surprised
to see Swinton's name on Endgame's IMDb page.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.859
Following her death, Doctor Strange wielded
the artifact known as the Eye of Agamotto,

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.640
which was revealed to be the Time Stone.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:27.380
The Ancient One's reappearance has fueled
fan theories that time travel will play a

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:29.000
major role in Endgame.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.980
In the first act of Infinity War, Wong joins
the fight against the invading Black Order.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.060
Once Doctor Strange is kidnapped, however,
Wong abruptly exits the remainder of the film's

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.540
action to protect the Sanctum Sanctorum.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:48.259
While Wong's fate post-snap is never fully
revealed, the actor has confirmed his participation

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.140
in Endgame.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:54.590
Assuming this means that Wong is alive and
well, this character could wind up being surprisingly

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:55.840
crucial to 
the plot.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.880
"Wong you're invited to my wedding."

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:07.990
Doctor Strange is conspicuously left out of
the confirmed cast for Endgame.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:13.260
When last we saw him in Infinity War, he was
disintegrating to dust while also hinting

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:14.520
at a larger plan.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.430
In Doctor Strange, Wong was the keeper of
the mystical library in Kamar-Taj and was

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:23.680
responsible for schooling Strange on the nature
of the Time Stone encased within the Eye of

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.440
Agamotto.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:30.060
As perhaps the last hero standing with in-depth
knowledge of the Infinity Stones, and significant

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:34.890
experience wielding the Time Stone, Wong may
be the one to bring Benedict Cumberbatch back

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.840
to the Endgame call sheet after all.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:42.660
Remember back in Iron Man 3 when Tony Stark
wound up in the garage of young Harley Keener?

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:43.440
"Freeze.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.140
Don't move.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.680
You got me."

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:53.560
While the character served the narrative of
Iron Man 3 and comedic sensibilities of director

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:58.880
Shane Black, what place could this kid now
a teenager possibly have in Endgame?

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:04.520
With rampant speculation that Endgame could
be Robert Downey Jr.'s final MCU appearance,

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:08.820
certain theories suggest that Keener could
make an appearance for Tony Stark's funeral.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:13.280
Others theorize that Stark could be looking
to pass the torch, and perhaps Keener could

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.240
be in line for the Iron Man mantle.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:21.850
Nearly every one of the Guardians of the Galaxy
perished in Infinity War only Rocket remains

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:22.800
of the core group.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:26.980
Star-Lord, Drax, Mantis, and Groot were all
taken in the culling.

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:32.460
It seems the Infinity Gauntlet affected an
unfair percentage of Guardians until you remember

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:36.409
that Star-Lord totally blew it on Titan.

00:03:36.409 --> 00:03:41.600
"No you didn't"

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:47.640
Maybe that's why he's the only one of these
characters not listed on Endgame's IMDb page.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:52.760
Mantis, Groot, and Drax are all confirmed
to be appearing according to that cast list.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:59.320
Gamora was also killed by Thanos in Infinity
War, though not by the snap instead, she was

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:04.580
offered as a sacrifice on planet Vormir by
Thanos in order to acquire the Soul Stone.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:08.120
We do see Gamora one more time in Infinity
War, however.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.680
Once Thanos has completed his goal of wiping
out half the life in the universe with the

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:17.700
Infinity Gauntlet, he appears in a dreamlike
dimension confronted by a young Gamora.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:22.600
The scene is bathed in an eerie orange light,
the same color as the Soul Stone.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:28.060
Speaking to children at Iowa City's City High,
co-director Joe Russo confirmed that this

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:33.000
scene actually takes place within the Stone
— or perhaps a pocket dimension created

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:33.520
by it.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.970
If Gamora is in this purgatory-like place
within the Soul Stone, is it possible that

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:40.560
the other dusted characters are also within
the orange realm?

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:46.900
Despite their apparent deaths in Ant-Man and
the Wasp, current and former Wasps, Hope and

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:53.200
Janet Van Dyne, are both listed on Endgame's
IMDb, though notably, Hank Pym isn't on the

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:53.700
list.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:58.520
According to Peyton Reed, who directed Ant-Man
and the Wasp, his film's timeline was left

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.130
intentionally ambiguous.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:05.400
"We liked the idea of the structure where,
in true Ant-Man style, everybody has closure

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:10.430
and everything's tied together and almost
in too neat of a bow at the end.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:14.960
Then to BANG — give the audience a gut punch
right after the main credits.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.400
That felt like our movie's tone and the way
of dealing with that."

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:23.030
In that credits sequence, just before Scott
hops into the Quantum Realm, Janet gives him

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:25.199
a potentially loaded warning:

00:05:25.199 --> 00:05:27.410
"And don't get sucked into a time vortex.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.940
We won't be able to save you,"

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:35.440
Could Scott Lang stuck in the Quantum Realm
possibly find a way to access different points

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.160
in time using a vortex?

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:42.630
Actor Frank Grillo has confirmed that Crossbones
makes an appearance in Endgame.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:48.169
The boney bad guy hasn't appeared in the MCU
since the opening sequence of 2016's Captain

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:51.540
America: Civil War, when he detonated a bomb
on himself.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.620
"And you're coming with me"

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:05.720
Speaking during a podcast interview with UFC
Unfiltered, Grillo said:

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:10.169
"He makes an appearance in the next Avengers
movie, but it's a flashback."

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:13.640
What's interesting here is Grillo's use of
the term "flashback."

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:18.000
Crossbones' appearance may very well be a
standard narrative flashback.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:23.200
But it could also be a lot more, given all
the time travel rumors surrounding not only

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:28.310
the Time Stone, but Ant-Man and The Wasp's
mid-credits sequence that leaves Ant-Man stuck

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:29.620
in the Quantum Realm.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:36.100
We all know Spidey is due back for his second
solo MCU film in Spider-Man: Far From Home.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:41.460
However, considering that the last time we
saw Peter Parker he wasn't feeling so good,

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:45.900
it's still kind of surprising to see his name
listed with the confirmed cast.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:50.290
Evidently, something gets Peter Parker back
from the great beyond in time for his field

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:51.600
trip in Far from Home.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:56.460
But fans believe that the trailer for Far
from Home hints at the death of another character

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:58.300
in Endgame: Tony Stark.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:03.840
Not only is Stark completely absent from the
Far From Home trailer, but some say Spider-Man's

00:07:03.849 --> 00:07:08.590
decision not to bring his Spidey Suit with
him on his trip is further evidence of Iron

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:11.920
Man's demise, and Peter's need to get some
distance from that grief.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:17.990
Of all of the terrible downfalls that occured
in Infinity War, perhaps nobody had a harsher

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:21.780
demise than Wanda Maximoff, a.k.a. Scarlet
Witch.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.360
Wanda uses her powers to pull the Mind Stone
from the Vision's head and destroy it.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:32.280
However, Thanos spoils her sacrifice by using
the Time Stone to rewind time and just get

00:07:32.289 --> 00:07:33.280
the stone anyway.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:38.220
On top of that, the snap turns Scarlet Witch
to dust just a few moments later.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:43.419
Despite all that, Elizabeth Olsen is slated
to reprise her role in Endgame.

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:45.840
According to Olsen, her situation won't improve.

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:51.280
Speaking on a panel at ACE Comic Con in Chicago,
Olsen cryptically warned that it was only

00:07:51.289 --> 00:07:52.660
going to get worse.

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:59.180
Sebastian Stan's Winter Soldier and his friendship
with Chris Evans' Captain America has been

00:07:59.189 --> 00:08:02.949
an emotional fulcrum for the MCU narrative
in recent years.

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:07.889
In Captain America: Civil War, the fight between
Cap and Tony was much deeper and much more

00:08:07.889 --> 00:08:09.520
personal than politics.

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:14.300
It took the bigger debate of the Sokovia Accords
and boiled it down to fighting for the soul

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.620
of Bucky Barnes.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:20.860
With Bucky reduced to ash in Infinity War,
how does Sebastian Stan find himself back

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:23.370
for Endgame as Winter Soldier?

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:27.439
Appearing on The Late Late Show with James
Corden, the host asked Stan if he could explain

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.700
how he came back for Avengers: Endgame.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.840
Stan had a coy reply for Corden:

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:33.220
"Bucky's dead.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.140
Happy New Year.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.480
That's it.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:37.500
That's all I got."

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.860
Darn these Marvel secrets!

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.760
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.860
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
superhero films are coming soon.

